hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"22282","Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Said, he said: Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, passed by Hassan while he was reciting in the mosque, and he glanced at him. He said: I used to recite while in it was one better than you. Then he turned to Abu Hurayra and said: Did you hear the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Respond on my behalf; O Allah, support him with the Holy Spirit? He said: Yes."
"22283","Yala narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abd al-Rahman, he said: Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, passed by Hassan while he was reciting poetry in the mosque. He said: In the mosque of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, do you recite poetry? He said: I used to recite while in it was one better than you, or: I used to recite in it while in it was one better than you."
"22284","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Ibrahim, meaning Ibn Sad, narrated to us, Ibn Shihab narrated to us, from Said ibn al-Musayyab, he said: Umar passed by Hassan while he was reciting in the mosque, and he said: Mah. Hassan said to him: I used to recite while in it was one better than you. He said: So Umar left knowing that he means the Messenger of Allah."
